==Personality==
Like all [[Nosedeenian (Classic)|Nosedeenians]], Buzzshock is prone to mischievousness or amusement. He always laughs whenever he moves around or fights.<ref name="TCoM">''[[The Color of Monkey]]''</ref>

==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
CIU (344).png|Bio-Electrokinesis
MaxMonster253.png|Energy Absorption
TCoM (61).png|Electricity Conductivity/Electricity Immunity
MaxMonster243.1.png|Self-Electromorphosis/Electroporation
TWB (478).png|Flight/Enhanced Speed
TWB (489).png|Levitation
MaxMonster232.1.png|Enhanced Reflexes
</gallery>
Buzzshock is like a living battery, able to store and release massive amounts of electricity within his body. The amount stored corresponds with his vitality; he gets energetic and hyper when full of electricity<ref name="TT">''[[Tourist Trap]]''</ref><ref>''[[Cough It Up]]''</ref><ref name="TCoM"/> and sleepy when deprived of it.<ref name="AJftP" />

Buzzshock can both project the electricity stored inside his body outward and absorb external electricity inward, primarily by using his hands.<ref name="B10k" /> He also has electrokinesis, and is able to control any electricity around him, allowing him to draw in electricity from far away or link himself to other [[Nosedeenian (Classic)|Nosedeenian]]s on a chain of lightning.<ref name="TT"/> He can absorb all the energy from a city block in a matter of seconds,<ref name="AJftP" /> and as a result of absorbing, his electric attacks become more powerful.<ref name="MM">''[[Max's Monster]]''</ref>

Not only is Buzzshock immune to electricity,<ref name="TCoM" /> he can convert parts of his body or his entire body into pure electricity, and travel across certain things, such as phone lines and pipes.<ref name="TT" /><ref name="MM" /> Using this ability, Buzzshock can inhabit electrical devices, controlling them from the inside, and in some cases powering them. He can also cause electrical technology to malfunction and fry when he passes through them.<ref name="TT" />

If Buzzshock absorbs enough energy, he can duplicate himself one or many times, as demonstrated by other Nosedeenians.<ref name="TT" /><ref name="AJftP" />{{Refn|[[:File:Buzzshock Must Learn To Duplicate.png]]|group = MW}} He can also duplicate if he is forcibly bisected, in which his two parts will regenerate and become two whole Nosedeenians.<ref name="TT" />

Buzzshock can naturally fly and levitate, and can also do so by turning his entire body or parts of it into electricity.<ref name="ATTWB">''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref><ref name="TCoM" />

Buzzshock is surprisingly strong for his size, as a Nosedeenian was able to lift an adult [[Human (Classic)|human]] several feet above the ground by their underwear.<ref name="TT" />

Buzzshock has enhanced reflexes, as shown when he quickly reacted and jumped over [[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil]]'s hand when he attacked him.<ref name="MM" />

Buzzshock can emit a sonic scream capable of shattering glass, as demonstrated by other Nosedeenians.<ref name="TT" />

==Weaknesses==
[[File:MaxMonster258.png|thumb|Small Size]]
Buzzshock can be insulated with rubber-sheeted blankets, as demonstrated with other [[Nosedeenian (Classic)|Nosedeenian]]s.<ref name="AJftP" />

Buzzshock can be trapped in something made of a non-conductive material, such as glass, as demonstrated with other Nosedeenians.<ref name="TT" />

Buzzshock's energy can be absorbed by a species such as [[Conductoid]]s, as demonstrated with other Nosedeenians.<ref name="AJftP">''[[A Jolt From the Past]]''</ref> If Buzzshock runs out of energy, he will be unable to stay awake.<ref name="AJftP"/>

Buzzshock's small size can be a disadvantage against a bigger, stronger opponent like Phil.<ref name="MM" />

==History==
===Omniverse=== 
*In ''[[Max's Monster]]'', Buzzshock was unlocked by [[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil]] so he could feed off him. He then recharged a [[Null Void Projector]] to defeat Phil by sending him back to the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]].
*In ''[[Cough It Up]]'', Buzzshock defeated [[SixSix (Classic)|SixSix]], but was defeated by [[SevenSeven]].
*In ''[[Rook Tales]]'', Buzzshock failed to take off [[Rook Ben|Young One]]'s tail.
*In ''[[The Color of Monkey]]'', Buzzshock battled [[Liam]] and [[Suemungousaur]].

===[[Original Future Timeline|Original Future]]===
*Buzzshock first appeared in ''[[Ben 10,000 (Episode)|Ben 10,000]]'', where he defeated [[Dr. Animo (Original Future)|Dr. Animo]].
*In ''[[Ken 10]]'', [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken]] as Buzzshock attempted to fight [[Mot Snikrep]] before the latter was frozen by [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] as [[Arctiguana]]. Later, Ken as Buzzshock briefly battled [[Kevin 11,000]] before the former reverted.

===Bad Ben's Timeline=== 
*In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', [[Bad Ben|Bad]] Buzzshock chased an Omnitrixless [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]] only to be sent back to his own timeline by [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] as [[Clockwork]].

