==Trivia== 
*Despite appearing in the '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' intro, Buzzshock was unavailable for [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] until ''[[Max's Monster]]''.
**Before this, Buzzshock appeared in the non-canon '''Ultimate Alien''' comic ''[[Black Knight's Flight]]''.
***'''Ultimate Alien''' Buzzshock also appears in [[Super Hero Time|''Super Hero Time'']].
**Buzzshock and [[Rath (Classic)|Rath]] are the only aliens to have been unlocked by electromagnetic interference.
*Like [[Frankenstrike]], [[Snare-Oh]], Murk [[Upchuck]], and [[Arctiguana]], Buzzshock appeared in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', but he did not appear in ''[[A New Dawn]]''.
*Buzzshock is one of five aliens featured in '''Omniverse''' who generate green electricity; the others being [[Upgrade (Classic)|Upgrade]], Frankenstrike, [[Brainstorm]], and [[Nanomech]].
*Buzzshock is the only one of the three aliens originally exclusive to [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] that is not repurposed from Perk Upchuck's concept art.
*Buzzshock was designed by [[Dave Johnson]] in the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]'''.{{Refn|[[:File:Dave Designed Upgrade and Buzzshock.png]]|group = TNP}} Buzzshock's '''Omniverse''' design originally had a more rotund physique as well as a positive (+) or negative (-) symbol on either his chest or forehead.{{Refn|[[:File:Buzzshock Concept Art by Derrick J. Wyatt.png]]|group = ca}}

